From: kimchaily <ly.kimchai@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 12:41:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add diagram color theme setting (auto/light/dark)

Adds a `bpmn-io.theme` setting to control the diagram canvas theme:

- `auto` (default): follows the active VS Code color theme. VS Code keeps
  a `vscode-dark`/`vscode-light` class in sync on the webview body, so
  this tracks the workbench live with no extra JavaScript.
- `light`: always render on a light background (previous behaviour).
- `dark`: always render on a dark background.

The diagram is rendered black-on-white by bpmn-js; the dark theme inverts
luminance while preserving hue (hue-rotate(180deg)) so user-defined
element colors stay recognizable and the popup/search menus darken too.

Changing the setting is pushed to open editors live via a
`onDidChangeConfiguration` listener, without reopening them.
